  <section class="py-16 md:py-24 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">

      <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl md:text-4xl text-ink mb-2">Terms and Conditions</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm mb-10">Last updated: November 2026</p>

      <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">

        <p>These terms apply to anyone who uses ddlandworksllc.com or contacts D&amp;D Land Works LLC about excavation, grading, land clearing, drainage, foundation excavation, trenching, driveway repair, or septic work.</p>

        <h2>1. Using this website</h2>
        <p>This site provides information about D&amp;D Land Works and lets you request a free estimate. You may use it for lawful purposes only. We may change, update, or take down any page at any time without notice.</p>

        <h2>2. Estimates are not contracts</h2>
        <p>A free estimate from D&amp;D Land Works is based on information available at the time of the site visit — ground conditions, access, slope, soil, drainage, and what you describe. Estimates can change once work begins if site conditions differ from what was visible during the visit.</p>
        <p>An estimate is not a binding contract. Work begins only when both parties have signed a written agreement.</p>

        <h2>3. Scope changes during a project</h2>
        <p>If the scope of work changes after a contract is signed — because of unexpected underground conditions, changes you request, or access issues that weren't visible during the estimate — we'll discuss those changes with you before proceeding. Additional work is priced separately.</p>

        <h2>4. Your responsibility to know your property</h2>
        <p>You are responsible for knowing your property lines and telling D&amp;D Land Works about any underground utilities, septic lines, wells, irrigation, or other buried infrastructure before work begins. D&amp;D Land Works is not responsible for damage to utilities or lines that were not disclosed or marked before excavation.</p>
        <p>Call 811 (Oregon One Call) before any digging project.</p>

        <h2>5. Permits</h2>
        <p>Depending on your project, permits may be required. It is your responsibility to obtain required permits unless we have agreed in writing to handle permitting as part of the project. D&amp;D Land Works holds Oregon CCB license #261742 and DEQ certification PLC# 39996 for septic work.</p>

        <h2>6. Payment</h2>
        <p>Payment terms are stated in the written contract for each project. Invoices not paid by the due date may be subject to a late fee. D&amp;D Land Works reserves the right to stop work on unpaid accounts.</p>

        <h2>7. No warranty on third-party materials</h2>
        <p>D&amp;D Land Works does not manufacture gravel, rock, fill, or other materials. We pass through any manufacturer or supplier warranties where available but make no independent warranty on materials supplied by third parties.</p>

        <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>D&amp;D Land Works is not liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages — including loss of use of your property — arising from services or from use of this website. Our total liability for any claim is limited to the amount paid for the specific service at issue.</p>

        <h2>9. Governing law</h2>
        <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the state of Oregon. Any dispute will be resolved in Lane County, Oregon.</p>

        <h2>10. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms at any time. Changes take effect when posted on this page with a new date. If you have an active contract with D&amp;D Land Works, the terms of that contract govern your project.</p>

